hostname originator
!
ip routing
!
interface Loopback0
   ip address 10.0.0.1/32
!
interface Loopback1
   ip address 10.1.1.1/24
!
interface Loopback2
   ip address 10.1.2.1/24
!
interface Loopback3
   ip address 10.1.3.1/24
!
interface Loopback4
   ip address 10.1.4.1/24
!
interface Ethernet1
   description to aggregator:eth1
   no switchport
   ip address 10.1.12.1/30
!
! ============================================================
! YOUR TASKS ON ORIGINATOR
! ============================================================
!
! TASK 1 — Base BGP, advertise all component prefixes
!   configure
!   router bgp 65001
!      bgp router-id 10.0.0.1
!      neighbor 10.1.12.2 remote-as 65002
!      !
!      address-family ipv4
!         neighbor 10.1.12.2 activate
!         network 10.0.0.1/32
!         network 10.1.1.0/24
!         network 10.1.2.0/24
!         network 10.1.3.0/24
!         network 10.1.4.0/24
!      !
!
!   Verify on aggregator: show bgp ipv4 unicast
!   All four /24s should be present with AS-path "65001".
!
! TASK 2 — Selective withdrawal (simulate a route going down)
!   To test aggregation behavior, remove one of the component routes:
!
!   router bgp 65001
!      address-family ipv4
!         no network 10.1.4.0/24
!      !
!
!   Observe: on aggregator, what happens to the aggregate?
!   (If aggregate-address requires all four to be present, removing one
!    may withdraw the aggregate. Depends on your configuration.)
!
!   Restore it after testing:
!      network 10.1.4.0/24
!
! NOTE: The "network" statement requires a matching route in the routing table.
! The loopback interfaces create directly connected routes, which satisfies this.
! ============================================================
end
